{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on `e9f00f3f`, the C4 loader draft.\n\n1. The draft arm. A request with a stored draft shows as\n   `is: \"draft\"` with `slot` and `values`, the present fields. A\n   page then renders one draft in one way before and after a\n   submit, and no partial act claims the type `AskedOf`. Change\n   the two assertions. Each still pins the place: \"handoff\" and\n   \"eight\" read item 0 from `slot` and the text from `values`.\n2. Change the assertion, and not to \"the next published view\".\n   Under `0967101f` no view depends on the fold. The case pins two\n   things. First: every published view that holds the entry shows\n   the request as recorded, read from the view. Second: the stored\n   record reaches `accepted` when the background step ends. Wait\n   for that step with a barrier that the test owns, and add no\n   sleep. Rename the case to say what it now pins.\n3. Yes. Narrow at each reader, and add no compatibility field.\n   Each arm of the list carries `is`, so a reader narrows with one\n   switch: give the request arm `is: \"request\"` in the list. Name\n   each changed reader in the END act.\n4. Yes to the row and to the rest of the view. No to the name.\n   The row is a held intention with the reason\n   `another-definition`, beside `another-descriptor`. It holds the\n   key and the stored definition digest, and no values. `restore`\n   stops with `definition-mismatch`, the stop that\n   `refineDraft` names today, and `dismiss` removes the row. The\n   definition check stays first, so a row that differs in both\n   shows `another-definition`. One case pins the row and pins that\n   the other rows of the same batch publish.\n\nThe seventh amendment takes item 4 into section 6: the held arm\nhas three reasons.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}